## Team Conventions [ORG-WIDE + CUSTOMIZE]

### Code Style [ORG-WIDE]
- All files use 2-space indentation unless a language-specific linter overrides this.
- TypeScript: strict mode enabled; no `any` without a comment explaining why.
- Python: PEP 8; type hints required on all public functions.
- Go: standard `gofmt` formatting; no underscore-prefixed exported identifiers.
- All exported functions and classes must have documentation comments.
- Maximum file length: 400 lines. If a file exceeds this, split it.

### Naming Conventions [ORG-WIDE]
- Functions: camelCase (TS/JS/Java), snake_case (Python/Go).
- Classes/types: PascalCase in all languages.
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.
- Database columns: snake_case.
- Environment variables: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE with project prefix (e.g., PAYMENTS_DB_URL).

### Project-Specific Conventions [CUSTOMIZE]
